      <title>Squeak 2.23.32</title>
      <pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:24:49 +0000</pubDate>
      <sparkle:version>22332</sparkle:version>
      <sparkle:shortVersionString>2.23.32</sparkle:shortVersionString>
      <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
      <description><![CDATA[<!DOCTYPE html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><style>html{color-scheme:light dark}body{font:13px/1.5 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'SF Pro Text',system-ui,sans-serif;color:#18181b;background:transparent;margin:0;padding:4px 2px}ul{margin:0 0 10px;padding-left:18px}li{margin:0 0 6px}p{margin:0 0 10px}h4{font-size:12px;font-weight:600;color:#52525b;margin:16px 0 6px;padding-top:10px;border-top:1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.08)}code{font:12px ui-monospace,'SF Mono',monospace;background:rgba(0,0,0,.06);padding:1px 4px;border-radius:6px}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#f4f4f5}h4{color:#a1a1aa;border-top-color:rgba(255,255,255,.12)}code{background:rgba(255,255,255,.1)}}</style></head><body><ul><li>A chat whose turn has ended but whose ducklings or background shells are still running keeps its working look in the sidebar, its tab, Home and the palette, so a busy stream never looks finished.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.31</h4><ul><li>A message you steer in while the agent waits on a helper now says which helper ("Waiting for Map recording features…"), with a Send now button that stops that helper and hands your message to the agent straight away.</li><li>Rename a thread right where its name is: choose Rename… (or double-click a chat in the sidebar), type, Return saves and Esc cancels. No more dialog.</li><li>New chats name themselves in a few words ("Merge Everything and Clean Repo") instead of showing your whole first message.</li><li>The terminal is never blank: ⌘J shows and hides the same live tab, closing the last tab or exiting its shell opens a fresh one, and a shell that stops at once says so with a button to start another.</li></ul><h4>Also in 2.23.30</h4><ul><li>Squeak's own colours: the dark and light greys are rebuilt from the duck's palette, a touch warmer, with easier-to-read secondary text (light mode's grey text now meets contrast).</li><li>Ready for Squeak's new chat words: chats waiting on you, a plan, an answer or stopping show correctly from the updated session host, and older chats keep working.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
